Value TABLE (Interface)
Value INTERFACE (\S+)
Value PROCESS_ID (\S+)
Value AREA (\S+)
Value ADDRESS (\S+)
Value COST (\S+)
Value STATE (\S+)
Value NEIGHBORS (\S+)
Value BAD_ROW (\S.*?)

# One record per line of "show ip ospf interface brief" (campus-wan lab, IOS-XE 17): the
# table header (TABLE), an interface row, or another line led by an interface name
# (BAD_ROW). Topology checks the order and the values (rules_tables.ospf_interfaces).
Start
  ^\s*${TABLE}\s+PID\s+Area\s+IP Address/Mask\s+Cost\s+State\s+Nbrs F/C\s*$$ -> Record
  ^\s*${INTERFACE}\s+${PROCESS_ID}\s+${AREA}\s+${ADDRESS}\s+${COST}\s+${STATE}\s+${NEIGHBORS}\s*$$ -> Record
  ^\s*${INTERFACE}\s+${BAD_ROW}\s*$$ -> Record
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error "unrecognized ospf interface line"
